WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.120
Covid-19 has encouraged many of us
to look at how we might optimise

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.760
our immune responses,
through supplements or superfoods.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.200
But is it even possible to alter how
the body responds to disease

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.280
through an immune-boosting pill
or by eating blueberries?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.200
And what about the people
who take it even further?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.080
The biohackers experimenting
with procedures such as

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.600
faecal transplants -

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.280
basically taking someone
else's poo as a medicine

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.480
in an attempt to cure
a range of ills.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.840
Dangerous experimentation
or smart science?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.600
The immune system is part
of an interconnected system,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.840
running all the way through our body.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.600
Involving all our tissues,
from our skin,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.880
all the way through to our toes.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.800
And in fact, the gut has one

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.120
of the largest resident populations

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.360
of immune cells in our body.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.440
Most of the body's immune cells are
found in the lining of the intestine,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.960
and the microbes in our gut
play a crucial role

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.680
in keeping those immune cells
of our body healthy.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.880
And they do that by providing
the key chemical signals

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.680
that they get once they digest

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.280
the good foods that we eat.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.640
So a healthy gut microbiome

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.440
is absolutely critical
to a healthy immune system.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.640
The immune system is considered
to be an organ.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.280
But unlike ever other organ
in your body,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.640
it's one where components

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.680
of the system

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.000
can migrate around the body.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.720
You don't expect that with cells
from your lungs,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.640
from your spleen,
or any other solid organ.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.800
But the beauty of
the immune system

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.920
is it has a property
of immuno-surveillance.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.440
Immunological surveillance is when
the cells of the immune system

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.680
come together to coordinate
a response to an external threat

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.200
such as disease.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.240
For example, your lymph nodes,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.000
the glands that swell up
when you are sick,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.120
are a sign of your immune
system at work.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.000
We often hear messages encouraging
us to boost our immune system.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.160
So, could we just take a pill
to do that?

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.440
When you do meet
an infectious threat,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.920
our immune response
has to react quickly -

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.680
to contain the threat
and eradicate it.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.840
And you don't want it to stay on,
because if it says on, it's damaging.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.400
And that is what happens in allergy
and autoimmune disease,

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.120
which are over-reactivity
of the immune response.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.840
So there is no wonder pill that is
going to restore and boost one part

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.240
of the immune response
to help us be super-powered,

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.800
because it's all so interconnected,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.560
and the risks of getting it wrong
are really quite dramatic.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.320
So, instead of boosting
our immune system,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.680
we should focus on supporting it.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.600
Everything that we know already
which is good for our health

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.600
will also benefit our immune system.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.720
More exercise,
taken at regular intervals,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.920
has been shown to boost
your immune function.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.760
That's been shown,
and that's published data.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.040
Unfortunately, the modern lifestyle

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.560
is not very good
for our immune system.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.600
Our diets of convenience foods

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.840
and fatty foods
that are low in fibre

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.680
alongside sedentary lifestyles
with little exercise,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
high stress and not too much sleep -
too much screen time.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.360
All of these combine
to make our immune response

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.280
not work as it should.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.600
Getting enough sleep
and reducing stress

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.920
can help our immune system
operate at an optimal level.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.520
And even though one blueberry
won't work miracles,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.040
getting a variety of the right foods,
is very important.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.760
To help your immunity you need
to be feeding up your gut microbes,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.560
and the best way to do this
is to make them more diverse -

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.480
give them more species.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.360
And I recommend 30 different
types of plant a week,

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.840
which gives you all
the fibre you should need.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.960
Secondly, you should pick plants
to eat that are high in polyphenols.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.520
These are the chemicals that
are naturally found in plants

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.160
that are actually rocket fuel
for your gut microbes.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.160
So things like
brightly coloured berries,

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.280
strong flavours like coffee beans,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.000
dark chocolate and even red wine
contain polyphenols.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.120
So, if what you eat and your gut is
so important for your immune system,

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.080
why are some people transplanting
other people's poo

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.840
into their own stomachs?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.720
Faecal microbial transplant
or, colloquially, a poo transplant,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.760
is taking a sample of a stool
from a normal person

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.680
and putting it into someone
who is unwell.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.120
This has been done
for several decades

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.720
for very bad infections of the bowel,
like Clostridium difficile,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.560
and it cures 90% of people.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.000
And it's been since started to be
used in a number of other conditions.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.800
This is a fascinating area
of research,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.640
but definitely not to be tried
at home, says Tim.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.680
I think this is an exciting
new form of therapy,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.320
but it's always best to do this
within the confines

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.920
of a medical clinic,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.280
where things can be supervised
and the risk of side effects

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.000
or infection is extremely low.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.360
There are some people who take risks
and do do it at home,

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.520
and those risks will be
multiplied considerably.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.440
There's a lot of hype about
faecal transplants,

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:08.160
and you mustn't believe people who
say that it works with everything,

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.080
in everybody, it certainly doesn't,

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.760
and there are many failures
in clinical trials.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:16.000
One of the ways we can
effectively and safely manipulate

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.640
our immune responses
is through vaccination.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.800
What a vaccine is doing
is essentially giving you

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.120
the parts of the germ that will
stimulate the immune response,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.960
without actually getting
the full blown infection.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.680
Another thing that we can do,

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.880
is actually try to switch
the immune response off.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.240
For some diseases we don't want
a powerful immune response,

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.600
because that's what's causing
the damage.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.720
This is exactly what's done in
diseases like rheumatoid arthritis,

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.560
multiple sclerosis,

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.200
or is also being investigated
in infections like Covid.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.320
The good news is, whilst there's
no one magic pill we can take

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.320
to boost our immune response,
the more scientists learn about

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.160
how our immune system works,
the more they can develop

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.120
new drug treatments and therapies
to combat a wide range of diseases.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:08.440
The knowledge of science is actually
leading to all sorts of wonderful

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:13.400
new possibilities to help treat us
and win the war against infection.

